  "executive_briefing": "As of mid-2026, the global tax landscape is defined by the transition from policy agreement to rigorous operational enforcement. Pillar Two remains the primary driver of international corporate tax policy, moving from legislative adoption to the complex phase of ETR (Effective Tax Rate) calculations and administrative filing. Trade policy is marked by persistent volatility as executive tariff actions\u2014such as the recent U.S. shifts\u2014compel corporations to integrate real-time duty tracking into their supply chain ERPs. Concurrently, digital tax administration is accelerating; mandatory e-invoicing and real-time transactional controls, exemplified by Singapore's InvoiceNow and global Peppol adoption, are replacing periodic reporting, creating a permanent state of audit-ready compliance for MNEs.",
